🚽 Test case: #193 -- copy-initializing a struct variable from a by-value
🚽 member of a different type (`gang Big g = b.s;` where `b.s` is a `gang
🚽 Small`) is rejected, not blindly memcpy'd -- the member-access
🚽 counterpart of struct_type_mismatch_copy_fail (PR #253 review,
🚽 finding 3). Sizes deliberately differ so a missing/inverted tag check
🚽 would be an out-of-bounds copy.
gang Small {
    rizz x;
};
gang Big {
    rizz a;
    rizz b;
    rizz c;
    rizz d;
};
gang Box {
    gang Small s;
};

skibidi main {
    gang Box b;
    gang Big g = b.s;
    bussin 0;
}
